{%- comment -%}
  Zo Veilig — cart guard. Ensures a package never sits in the live cart without its
  platform's one-time installation fee. A package is recognized by its own prepaid
  "Eerste 3 maanden" promo line (see Platform detection below), not by a
  subscription-type product — the plain package product is never added to cart under the
  prepaid line-item model (CLAUDE.md, Pricing pipeline).

  Climax (pricing.config.json activation.productHandle/sku, "Climax Instalatie", CL003):
  UNCHANGED behaviour. The Oplossingen and Vergelijk pakketten add-to-cart flows already add
  this fee alongside a package, but nothing stops it being removed afterwards in the cart, or
  a package reaching the cart through an entry point that doesn't add it — e.g. the standalone
  Shopify product page's default "Toevoegen aan winkelwagen" button (Dawn's stock buy-buttons,
  no custom wiring). On load, if a subscription line exists with no matching activation-fee
  line, it adds the fee and reloads — no ambiguity, one fixed fee, one correct answer. Skipped
  when a nami-install line is already present (a nami cart in good standing must never also
  pick up the flat climax fee).

  Nami (pricing.config.json installationOptions.nami.options, 3 differently-priced variants):
  this guard must NEVER pick one of the three for the customer — unlike the climax fee, there
  isn't one correct answer, only the customer's own choice on the Overzicht page (required
  radio group there, see sections/zv-checkout-overview.liquid). The only nami-specific fix
  applied here is a consistency dedupe: if more than one of the 3 nami-install variants is
  present at once (e.g. a stale line left behind by an interrupted swap), keep the most
  recently added and remove the rest, then reload. A cart with none of the three is left
  alone — that is the expected, correct state until the customer chooses.

  Platform detection (2026-09-22): under the prepaid line-item model the plain package
  product is never added to cart, so "is there a package here, and which platform is it"
  is now answered by the package's own "Eerste 3 maanden" promo line instead of a
  subscription-type line. That is strictly more reliable than what this script could do
  before: the promo variant ids are resolved server-side per platform, so unlike the old
  product_type check, a mixed cart's climax fee and nami choice are each evaluated on
  their own — no guessing from the Cart AJAX API, which still doesn't expose a line
  item's product.metafields (custom.finder_key) the way server-side Liquid does.

  Stray package line (2026-09-23): a subscription-type product should never reach the cart
  — the product page no longer renders a buy form for one (sections/main-product.liquid) —
  but if one arrives by any other route, it is swapped for that package's promo line rather
  than left to be charged. Its monthly price would otherwise be collected today, with no
  installation fee and nothing for Overzicht to identify the package by.

  The mapping is keyed on the line's product `handle`, not `custom.finder_key`: the Cart
  AJAX API doesn't expose product metafields the way server-side Liquid does, but it does
  expose the handle, and pricing.config.json carries each package's productHandle next to
  its promoProduct. Vista has no promo product, so a Vista line is left alone (it isn't
  purchasable anyway). After the swap the cart re-enters the normal flow: the reload runs
  this guard again, which then adds the climax activation fee if that's what's missing, or
  leaves a nami cart for the customer's own install choice on Overzicht.

  Silent no-op throughout if a variant id can't be resolved, or if a fetch fails (e.g.
  offline) — the caller also fails safe server-side (see zv-checkout-overview.liquid's
  cart_needs_activation gate, which blocks checkout regardless of whether this script runs).

  Params: activation_variant_id, sub_type, nami_geen_variant_id, nami_telefonisch_variant_id,
  nami_huis_variant_id, promo_inzicht_variant_id, promo_zeker_variant_id,
  promo_beschermd_variant_id, promo_alert_variant_id, promo_protect_variant_id, and the
  matching package product handles inzicht_handle, zeker_handle, beschermd_handle,
  alert_handle, protect_handle (passed explicitly because `render` doesn't inherit the
  caller's scope, same reason the variant ids are).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture zv_guard_pkg_map -%}
  {
    {{ inzicht_handle | json }}: {{ promo_inzicht_variant_id | json }},
    {{ zeker_handle | json }}: {{ promo_zeker_variant_id | json }},
    {{ beschermd_handle | json }}: {{ promo_beschermd_variant_id | json }},
    {{ alert_handle | json }}: {{ promo_alert_variant_id | json }},
    {{ protect_handle | json }}: {{ promo_protect_variant_id | json }}
  }
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- if activation_variant_id != blank or nami_geen_variant_id != blank or nami_telefonisch_variant_id != blank or nami_huis_variant_id != blank -%}
<script>
(function () {
  if (window.__zvCartGuardRan) return;
  window.__zvCartGuardRan = true;
  var ACTIVATION_ID = {{ activation_variant_id | json }};
  var SUB_TYPE = {{ sub_type | json }};
  var NAMI_IDS = [{{ nami_geen_variant_id | json }}, {{ nami_telefonisch_variant_id | json }}, {{ nami_huis_variant_id | json }}]
    .filter(function (id) { return id != null; })
    .map(String);
  // Promo line ids, split by which installation model their package uses.
  var PROMO_NAMI_IDS = [{{ promo_inzicht_variant_id | json }}, {{ promo_zeker_variant_id | json }}, {{ promo_alert_variant_id | json }}]
    .filter(function (id) { return id != null; })
    .map(String);
  var PROMO_CLIMAX_IDS = [{{ promo_beschermd_variant_id | json }}, {{ promo_protect_variant_id | json }}]
    .filter(function (id) { return id != null; })
    .map(String);
  // package product handle -> that package's promo variant id (see comment above).
  var PKG_HANDLE_TO_PROMO = {{ zv_guard_pkg_map }};

  window.fetch('/cart.js').then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(function (cart) {
    var items = (cart && cart.items) || [];
    var hasSub = items.some(function (it) { return it.product_type === SUB_TYPE; });
    var hasActivation = items.some(function (it) { return String(it.variant_id) === String(ACTIVATION_ID); });
    var namiLines = items.filter(function (it) { return NAMI_IDS.indexOf(String(it.variant_id)) !== -1; });
    var hasPromoNami = items.some(function (it) { return PROMO_NAMI_IDS.indexOf(String(it.variant_id)) !== -1; });
    var hasPromoClimax = items.some(function (it) { return PROMO_CLIMAX_IDS.indexOf(String(it.variant_id)) !== -1; });

    if (namiLines.length > 1) {
      var keepId = String(namiLines[namiLines.length - 1].variant_id);
      var updates = {};
      namiLines.forEach(function (it) {
        var vid = String(it.variant_id);
        if (vid !== keepId) updates[vid] = 0;
      });
      return window.fetch('/cart/update.js', {
        method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ updates: updates })
      }).then(function (r) { if (r.ok) window.location.reload(); });
    }

    // A climax package needs the one fixed activation fee - one correct answer, safe to
    // add. A nami package's install choice is never picked on the customer's behalf; the
    // required radio group on Overzicht is the only place that gets set.
    if (hasPromoClimax && !hasActivation) {
      return window.fetch('/cart/add.js', {
        method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ items: [{ id: ACTIVATION_ID, quantity: 1 }] })
      }).then(function (r) { if (r.ok) window.location.reload(); });
    }

    // A stray package line is swapped for that package's promo line (see comment above),
    // before any fee handling - the reload re-runs this guard, which then sorts the fee out.
    var strays = items.filter(function (it) {
      return it.product_type === SUB_TYPE && PKG_HANDLE_TO_PROMO[it.handle];
    });
    if (strays.length) {
      var removals = {};
      var additions = [];
      strays.forEach(function (it) {
        removals[String(it.variant_id)] = 0;
        var promoId = PKG_HANDLE_TO_PROMO[it.handle];
        var already = items.some(function (o) { return String(o.variant_id) === String(promoId); });
        if (!already && additions.every(function (a) { return String(a.id) !== String(promoId); })) {
          additions.push({ id: promoId, quantity: 1 });
        }
      });
      return window.fetch('/cart/update.js', {
        method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ updates: removals })
      })
        .then(function (r) {
          if (!r.ok) throw new Error(r.status);
          if (!additions.length) return r;
          return window.fetch('/cart/add.js', {
            method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ items: additions })
          });
        })
        .then(function (r) { if (r.ok) window.location.reload(); });
    }
  }).catch(function () { /* fail safe: server-side gate (Overzicht) still blocks checkout */ });
})();
</script>
{%- endif -%}
